---
import Component from "../../layouts/Component.astro"
import Anatomy from "../../components/Anatomy.astro"
import AutoExample from "../../components/AutoExample.astro"
import Conditional from "../../components/Conditional.astro"
import DocLink from "../../components/DocLink.astro"
import PropOrClass from "../../components/PropOrClass.astro"
import { Stepper as UIStepper } from "@opui/astro"

import StepperCSS from "@opui/css/components/stepper.css?raw"

import stepperApi from "../../component-api/stepper/api"

export const description =
  "Shows where someone is in a flow of steps, such as a checkout."
---

<Component
  description={description}
  slug="stepper"
  heroAnatomy
  apis={[{ title: "Stepper API", api: stepperApi }]}
  browserSupport={[
    "alt-text-generated-content",
    "container-queries",
    "container-style-queries",
    "has",
    "masks",
    "relative-color",
  ]}
  changelogPaths={[
    {
      path: "packages/opui/components/Stepper/Stepper.astro",
      type: "component",
    },
    { path: "src/docs/components/stepper.astro", type: "docs" },
    { path: "src/component-examples/stepper", type: "docs" },
    { path: "packages/opui/css/components/stepper.css", type: "css" },
    { path: "src/component-api/stepper", type: "api" },
  ]}
  installationTabs={[{ title: "stepper.css", code: StepperCSS, lang: "css" }]}
>
  <Fragment slot="title">Stepper</Fragment>
  <Fragment slot="preamble">
    Shows where someone is in a flow of steps, such as a checkout or an
    onboarding. The current step marks every step before it as complete. See
    also: <DocLink href="/components/progress" class="ui-link">Progress</DocLink
    >.
  </Fragment>

  <Fragment slot="anatomy">
    <Anatomy>
      <UIStepper
        current={1}
        items={[
          { description: "Name and email", href: "#basics", label: "Account" },
          { description: "Free or Pro", label: "Plan" },
          { description: "Card or invoice", label: "Payment" },
        ]}
        label="Sign-up steps"
        style="inline-size: 14rem"
      >
        <svg
          slot="check"
          xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
          width="24"
          height="24"
          viewBox="0 0 24 24"
          fill="none"
          stroke="currentColor"
          stroke-width="2"
          stroke-linecap="round"
          stroke-linejoin="round"
          ><path d="M18 6 7 17l-5-5"></path><path d="m22 10-7.5 7.5L13 16"
          ></path></svg
        >
      </UIStepper>
    </Anatomy>
  </Fragment>

  <section>
    <h2 id="basics">Basics</h2>
    <Conditional as="p">
      <Fragment slot="astro"
        >Set <code>current</code> to the index of the current step, from 0. Every
        step before it is complete. Completed steps with an <code>href</code> render
        a link back, the current and later steps render text.</Fragment
      >
      <Fragment slot="html"
        >Put <code>aria-current="step"</code> on the current <code>li</code>.
        Every step before it is complete, so moving that one attribute updates
        the whole stepper. Link the completed steps so people can go back.</Fragment
      >
      <Fragment slot="svelte"
        >Set <code>current</code> to the index of the current step, from 0. Every
        step before it is complete. Completed steps with an <code>href</code> render
        a link back, the current and later steps render text.</Fragment
      >
      <Fragment slot="vue"
        >Set <code>current</code> to the index of the current step, from 0. Every
        step before it is complete. Completed steps with an <code>href</code> render
        a link back, the current and later steps render text.</Fragment
      >
    </Conditional>

    <AutoExample name="Basics" />
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 id="sizes">Sizes</h2>
    <p>
      Use <PropOrClass prop='size="small"' class=".ui-small" /> for a smaller stepper.
    </p>

    <AutoExample name="Sizes" />
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 id="descriptions">Descriptions</h2>
    <Conditional as="p">
      <Fragment slot="astro"
        >Give a step a <code>description</code> for a short line under its label.</Fragment
      >
      <Fragment slot="html"
        >Add a <code>&lt;span class="ui-description"&gt;</code> after the label for
        a short line under it.</Fragment
      >
      <Fragment slot="svelte"
        >Give a step a <code>description</code> for a short line under its label.</Fragment
      >
      <Fragment slot="vue"
        >Give a step a <code>description</code> for a short line under its label.</Fragment
      >
    </Conditional>

    <AutoExample name="Descriptions" />
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 id="custom-checkmark">Custom checkmark</h2>
    <p>
      The default check is cut out of the marker, so it follows the theme. Swap
      it for any SVG with <code>--_check-icon</code>, and resize it with <code
        >--_check-size</code
      >.
    </p>

    <AutoExample name="CustomCheckIcon" />

    <Conditional as="p">
      <Fragment slot="astro"
        >To use your own icon component, pass it to the <code>check</code> slot. The
        stepper renders it in a <code>.ui-check</code> in every step, hidden from
        screen readers, and shows it on the completed ones. Steps you write in the
        default slot need their own <code
          >&lt;span class="ui-check" aria-hidden="true"&gt;</code
        >.</Fragment
      >
      <Fragment slot="html"
        >To use markup, such as an icon from your library, an <code>img</code> or
        an emoji, put it in a <code
          >&lt;span class="ui-check" aria-hidden="true"&gt;</code
        > first in each <code>li</code>. It shows on completed steps in place of
        the default check, in the marker's text color.</Fragment
      >
      <Fragment slot="svelte"
        >To use your own icon component, pass it to the <code>check</code> snippet.
        The stepper renders it in a <code>.ui-check</code> in every step, hidden from
        screen readers, and shows it on the completed ones. Steps you write in <code
          >children</code
        > need their own <code
          >&lt;span class="ui-check" aria-hidden="true"&gt;</code
        >.</Fragment
      >
      <Fragment slot="vue"
        >To use your own icon component, pass it to the <code>check</code> slot. The
        stepper renders it in a <code>.ui-check</code> in every step, hidden from
        screen readers, and shows it on the completed ones. Steps you write in the
        default slot need their own <code
          >&lt;span class="ui-check" aria-hidden="true"&gt;</code
        >.</Fragment
      >
    </Conditional>

    <AutoExample name="CustomCheck" />
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 id="vertical">Vertical</h2>
    <p>
      <PropOrClass prop='orientation="vertical"' class=".ui-vertical" /> stacks the
      steps. Use it for long labels or many steps.
    </p>

    <AutoExample name="Vertical" />
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 id="narrow-containers">Narrow containers</h2>
    <p>
      A stepper narrower than <code>32rem</code> turns vertical on its own. Drag the
      corner of the box to try it. The stepper measures its own width, so in a flex
      row give it one, for example with <code>flex: 1</code>.
    </p>
    <p>
      Browsers without container queries keep it horizontal, and the steps wrap.
    </p>

    <AutoExample name="Responsive" />
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 id="completed-label">Completed label</h2>
    <Conditional as="p">
      <Fragment slot="astro"
        >Screen readers announce a completed step as "Completed: Cart".
        Translate it with <code>completedLabel</code>, or for a whole language
        with <code>--_completed-label</code> and <code>:lang()</code>, as below.
        The stepper follows the text direction.</Fragment
      >
      <Fragment slot="html"
        >Screen readers announce a completed step as "Completed: Cart".
        Translate it with <code>--_completed-label</code>, for example for a
        whole language with <code>:lang()</code>. The stepper follows the text
        direction.</Fragment
      >
      <Fragment slot="svelte"
        >Screen readers announce a completed step as "Completed: Cart".
        Translate it with <code>completedLabel</code>, or for a whole language
        with <code>--_completed-label</code> and <code>:lang()</code>, as below.
        The stepper follows the text direction.</Fragment
      >
      <Fragment slot="vue"
        >Screen readers announce a completed step as "Completed: Cart".
        Translate it with <code>completedLabel</code>, or for a whole language
        with <code>--_completed-label</code> and <code>:lang()</code>, as below.
        The stepper follows the text direction.</Fragment
      >
    </Conditional>

    <AutoExample name="Translated" />
  </section>

  <Fragment slot="accessibility">
    <p>
      The stepper is an ordered list, so screen readers announce the number of
      steps and the position of each one. The numbers in the markers are hidden
      from them, so they aren't read twice.
    </p>
    <Conditional as="p">
      <Fragment slot="astro">Give it a name with <code>label</code>.</Fragment>
      <Fragment slot="html"
        >Give it a name with <code>aria-label</code>.</Fragment
      >
      <Fragment slot="svelte">Give it a name with <code>label</code>.</Fragment>
      <Fragment slot="vue">Give it a name with <code>label</code>.</Fragment>
    </Conditional>
    <p>
      <code>aria-current="step"</code> is announced as the current step. The completed
      steps get "Completed: " from the marker's alternative text (<a
        href="#completed-label">Completed label</a
      >). Browsers without alternative text for generated content read the
      numbers and "check mark" instead.
    </p>
    <p>
      A custom check is hidden from screen readers with <code
        >aria-hidden="true"</code
      >, so the announcement stays the same.
    </p>
    <p>
      In forced colors mode, completed markers are filled with <code
        >CanvasText</code
      >, the current marker gets a <code>Highlight</code> border, and the lines to
      later steps are <code>GrayText</code>.
    </p>
  </Fragment>
</Component>
